_sigmoid_gated_delta_rule) is gated on self.gqa_interleaved_layout, i.e. Qwen3-Next only. Qwen3.5 (this model) uses the non-interleaved q/k/v/z layout and is forced onto the generic split/rearrange Triton _forward_core path even though aiter's Triton GDN kernels are imported and available (GDN_AITER_TRITON_AVAILABLE true in baseline log warmup).\",\"source\":\"/opt/envs/wu1w/.../vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:1216-1230 (gate comment), 1572-1636\",\"expected_impact\":\"48 of 64 layers are GDN; a fused single-token decode conv+recurrent path could cut decode launch/rearrange overhead on the dominant layer class.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"layout mismatch would be numerically wrong; must verify fused_reshape kernel handles non-interleaved qkvz packing\",\"domain_tags\":[\"gdn\",\"decode\",\"aiter\",\"triton\"]},\n   {\"what\":\"ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN never enters the backend candidate list on gfx90a: _get_backend_priorities only appends it when is_aiter_found_and_supported(), which hard-requires get_cdna_version()>2 (CDNA3+). The backend itself (supports_head_size: head_size>=32, block MultipleOf(16), bfloat16) would accept this model's head_dim=256/block 784; it runs aiter's Triton unified_attention (same kernel family as the current TRITON_ATTN fallback but aiter-tuned).\",\"source\":\"/opt/envs/wu1w/.../vllm/platforms/rocm.py:481-495; _aiter_ops.py:145-153; v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py:41-70,146-148; baseline server.log:32,63\",\"expected_impact\":\"16/64 layers do full attention at hd256; aiter tuned Triton unified attention is the plausible faster path for the 1/4 full-attn layers.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"low (same math, different kernel)\",\"domain_tags\":[\"attention\",\"aiter\",\"gfx90a\"]},\n   {\"what\":\"AITER fused QK-norm+RoPE+KV-cache-update pass (fuse_qk_norm_rope_kvcache) is opt-in and off by default at every optimization level; on ROCm+AITER it is gated only by is_custom_op_enabled('rotary_embedding'), which fails because the baseline runs custom_ops=['none','+sparse_attn_indexer']. enable_qk_norm_rope_fusion is likewise default-False and needs +rotary_embedding. Qwen3.5 decoder = Qwen3NextAttention with per-head QK-norm + RoPE + KV-cache update on the 16 full-attn layers.\",\"source\":\"/opt/envs/wu1w/.../vllm/config/vllm.py:207-310 (OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL tables), config/compilation.py:1356-1367, platforms/rocm.py; compilation/passes/pass_manager.py:207-210; v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py:312-315 (fused_qk_norm_rope_kvcache_supported=rocm_aiter_ops.is_enabled()); baseline server.log:19\",\"expected_impact\":\"Fuses 3-4 elementwise kernels per attn layer into one AITER op on the hot decode path; classic gfx9 win.\",\"accuracy_risk\":\"low-medium (fusion numerics)\",\"domain_tags\":[\"fusion\",\"aiter\",\"compile_pass\"]}\n  ],\n  \"proposal_set\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"rocm-aiter-unified-attn-bridge\",\n    \"reason\": \"Bridge candidate #2: ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN is silently disqualified on gfx90a solely by the CDNA3-only is_aiter_found_and_supported() gate (get_cdna_version()>2) in platforms/rocm.py:_get_backend_priorities, even though the backend supports head_size>=32 (hd256 ok) and MultipleOf(16) blocks (784 ok) and its kernel is aiter's Triton unified_attention (works on CDNA2; the tree already ships an gfx90a carve-out helper is_aiter_attention_supported() for exactly this purpose, used for INT8 linear). Baseline runs ROCM_ATTN with its CK paged kernel rejected (head_dim 256 -> 'Cannot use ROCm custom paged attention kernel, falling back to Triton'), i.e. plain vLLM Triton attention. Freeform patch: use the gfx90a-inclusive predicate (or add --attention-backend ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN validation bridge) so the aiter-tuned kernel is selected for the 16 full-attn layers.\",\n    \"kb_evidence\": [],\n    \"pr_evidence\": [],\n    \"source_evidence\": [\n      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:481-495\",\n      \