   {\n    \"name\": \"gdn-decode-aiter-fastpath-noninterleaved\",\n    \"reason\": \"Bridge candidate #1 (patch work, highest expected value, medium risk): the AITER fused GDN single-token decode fast path exists and its kernels are loaded on this box, but _forward_core_rocm dispatches to it only when self.gqa_interleaved_layout (Qwen3-Next); this checkpoint is Qwen3.5 non-interleaved so all 48 GDN layers take the generic split/rearrange Triton path during decode (the dominant regime at conc=64/OSL=1024). Recon says the block is purely the layout predicate + the fused_reshape kernel's packing assumption — freeform specialist should verify aiter fused_reshape_causal_conv1d_update_single_token qkvz unpacking against the Qwen3.5 [q,k,v,z]-shard layout (prepare_gdn_attention_core_inputs shows the non-interleaved mapping) and bridge, or add an equivalent fused decode path; gate behind env for A/B.\",\n    \"kb_evidence\": [],\n    \"pr_evidence\": [],\n    \"source_evidence\": [\n      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:82-90,1216-1237,1572-1636\",\n      \"runs/baseline/.../server.log:29-31 (Triton GDN decode active)\"\n    ],\n    \"extra_envs\": {},\n    \"args_mode\": \"append\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"residual_questions\": [\n    \"KB: no recipe/pitfall entry yet for vllm 0.28.0+rocm723 gfx90a Qwen3.5 GDN — record whether aiter Triton unified_attention (hd256) beats plain vLLM Triton on CDNA2 after the next bench.\",\n    \"Does aiter.ops.triton.causal_conv1d_update_single_token.fused_reshape_causal_conv1d_update_single_token support non-interleaved qkvz (Qwen3.5) layout, or does its reshape hardcode interleaving? Needs kernel-source read of /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/aiter/ops/triton/.\",\n    \"Would --mamba-cache-dtype bfloat16 (--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16 is accepted by the fused-GDN state dtype whitelist FUSED_GDN_STATE_DTYPES) measurably cut GDN state bandwidth on this memor