{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_93c8c04dd011277f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"intent_type\": \"specialist_done\",\n3\t \"payload\": {\n4\t  \"confidence\": 0.7,\n5\t  \"domain\": \"static_recon_specialist\",\n6\t  \"empty\": false,\n7\t  \"gap_canonical_id\": \"gap.static_recon.prelude\",\n8\t  \"summary\": \"Recon of the LIVE serving tree (/opt/envs/wu1w/.../vllm via vllm-wu1w launcher; NOT /opt/envs/vllm) for gfx90a + INT8-W8A8 + bf16 Qwen3.5 hybrid-GDN. Baseline log confirms AiterInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel is already bridged+selected (no win there). Found 3 un-bridged switches: (1) ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN backend is silently disqualified on gfx90a by the CDNA3-only is_aiter_found_and_supported() priority gate although it supports hd>=32/blk%16/bf16 — baseline runs plain vLLM Triton attention for the 16 full-attn layers (hd256 kills the CK paged kernel); bypassable config-only via --attention-backend. (2) AITER fused QK-norm+RoPE+KV-cache pass (ROCm/AITER exists) default-False at every opt level + needs +rotary_embedding under custom_ops 'none'. (3) AITER fused GDN decode fast path exists but is gated to gqa_interleaved_layout (Qwen3-Next); Qwen3.5 (non-interleaved, 48 GDN layers = dominant decode cost) always takes the generic Triton path — patch candidate for freeform.\",\n9\t  \"new_findings\": [\n10\t   {\"what\": \"Live vllm source is /opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm (launched via /usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w), which differs from /opt/envs/vllm and already carries a gfx90a AITER INT8 linear bridge: is_linear_enabled() uses is_aiter_attention_supported() (on_gfx9, includes gfx90a) instead of the CDNA3-only @if_aiter_supported. Baseline server.log:28 'Selected AiterInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel' confirms it fires.\", \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/_aiter_ops.py:210-219,1833-1837; baseline server.log:28\", \"expected_impact\": \"Redirects all future recon/patch work to the correct tree; avoids re-proposing an already-bridged switch.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"none\", \"domain_tags\": [\"static_recon\", \"source_layout\", \"gfx90a\"]},\n11\t   {\"what\": \"ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN never enters candidate backends on gfx90a: platforms/rocm.py _get_backend_priorities only appends it under is_aiter_found_and_supported() = get_cdna_version()>2 (CDNA3+). The backend itself supports head_size>=32 (hd256 OK), block MultipleOf(16) (784 OK), bf16, and runs aiter's Triton unified_attention (arch-neutral, same kernel family as the fallback). Baseline therefore uses ROCM_ATTN whose CK custom paged kernel is rejected at hd256 ('Cannot use ROCm custom paged attention kernel, falling back to Triton implementation') = generic vLLM Triton for all 16 full-attn layers.\", \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:481-495; _aiter_ops.py:145-153; v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py:41-70,146-148; baseline server.log:32,63\", \"expected_impact\": \"AITER-tuned Triton attention on the 16/64 full-attn layers at conc=64 decode; explicit --attention-backend bypasses the priority gate and validate_configuration passes for this config.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"low (same attention math, different kernel)\", \"domain_tags\": [\"attention\", \"aiter\", \"gfx90a\"]},\n12\t   {\"what\": \"AITER fused QK-norm+RoPE+KV-cache-update pass (fuse_qk_norm_rope_kvcache, ROCm-gated) is default-False at ALL optimization levels and its last gate is_custom_op_enabled('rotary_embedding') fails because baseline runs custom_ops ['none','+sparse_attn_indexer']. When enabled via -ac it appends '+rotary_embedding' itself and runs QkNormRopeKvcacheFusionPass; the fused op executes via the aiter unified-attn impl's do_qk_norm_rope_kvcache_update (fused_qk_norm_rope_kvcache_supported = rocm_aiter_ops.is_enabled(), already true here).\", \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/config/vllm.py:207-216,225-310; config/compilation.py:272-295,956-963,1356-1367; compilation/passes/pass_manager.py:207-210; v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py:312-315\", \"expected_impact\": \"Fuses qknorm+rope+reshape_and_cache into one AITER kernel per full-attn layer, removing 3-4 elementwise launches/layer on the decode hot path.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"low-medium (fusion numerics; accuracy gate covers)\", \"domain_tags\": [\"fusion\", \"aiter\", \"compile_pass\"]},\n13\t   {\"what\": \"AITER GDN fused single-token decode fast path (_forward_core_decode_aiter: fused conv1d-update + fused_rearrange_sigmoid_gated_delta_rule, both aiter Triton) is dispatched only when self.gqa_interleaved_layout (Qwen3-Next). Qwen3.5's non-interleaved q/k/v/z packing is explicitly excluded by the gate comment ('Qwen3.5 ... must use the generic path'). 48 of 64 layers are GDN and decode is the dominant regime (conc=64, OSL=1024). Note: vllm _gdn_triton_kernels_importable() probes 'aiter.ops.triton.causal_conv1d_update_single_token' which resolves only via aiter's lazy module map (file lives at aiter/ops/triton/conv/).\", \"source\": \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py:78-90,1216-1237,1572-1636; _aiter_ops.py:1997-2018; aiter/ops/triton/__init__.py:149; baseline server.log:29-31\", \"expected_impact\": \"Largest untapped decode lever on this model class (48 GDN layers) if the fused kernels' reshape assumptions hold for non-interleaved packing.\", \"accuracy_risk\": \"medium: layout mismatch would corrupt state; kernel source must be read before patching\", \"domain_tags\": [\"gdn\", \"decode\", \"aiter\", \"qwen3_5\"]}\n14\t  ],\n15\t  \"proposal_set\": [\n16\t   {\n17\t    \"name\": \"bridge-rocm-aiter-unified-attn-hd256\",\n18\t    \"reason\": \"Bridge candidate: the aiter Triton unified-attention fast path exists and validates for this model (hd256>=32, block 784%16==0, bf16, causal) but is silently excluded from auto-selection on gfx90a solely by the CDNA3-only is_aiter_found_and_supported() (get_cdna_version()>2) priority gate in platforms/rocm.py:_get_backend_priorities — the same CDNA2-ism the tree already patched around for INT8 linear (is_aiter_attention_supported). Baseline runs generic vLLM Triton attention (CK paged kernel rejected at head_dim 256). Config-only bridge: explicit --attention-backend skips the priority list and goes straight to validate_configuration, which this model passes. If it starts and the log shows 'Using ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN backend (selected via --attention-backend)', the kernel-level A/B for the 16 full-attn layers is live.\",\n19\t    \"kb_evidence\": [],\n20\t    \"pr_evidence\": [],\n21\t    \"source_evidence\": [\n22\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/platforms/rocm.py:481-495 (_get_backend_priorities CDNA3 gate)\",\n23\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/_aiter_ops.py:145-153 (is_aiter_found_and_supported: get_cdna_version()>2)\",\n24\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py:41-70 (supports_head_size>=32, MultipleOf(16) blocks), :146-148 (aiter.ops.triton.unified_attention)\",\n25\t      \"session runs/baseline server.log:32,63 (ROCM_ATTN selected; custom paged attn rejected -> Triton)\"\n26\t    ],\n27\t    \"extra_args\": \"--attention-backend ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN\",\n28\t    \"args_mode\": \"append\",\n29\t    \"atomic\": false\n30\t   },\n31\t   {\n32\t    \"name\": \"bridge-aiter-qk-norm-rope-kvcache-fusion\",\n33\t    \"reason\": \"Atomic coupled bridge of the AITER fused QK-norm+RoPE+KV-cache-update pass: it exists for ROCm+AITER (enable_qk_norm_rope_kvcache = rocm_aiter_ops.is_enabled() && is_custom_op_enabled('rotary_embedding')) but is default-False at every optimization level AND the fused executor (do_qk_norm_rope_kvcache_update) lives on the aiter unified-attn impl, which gfx90a auto-selection silently never picks (CDNA3-only priority gate, see sibling proposal). Both switches must flip together or the pass matches but falls back unfused: (a) --attention-backend ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN; (b) --compilation-config replacing the base one (remove_args drops the inherited flag), keeping cudagraph_mode FULL_DECODE_ONLY and +sparse_attn_indexer, adding fuse_qk_norm_rope_kvcache and +rotary_embedding under the required 'none' base. Fuses 3-4 elementwise kernels per layer on the 16 full-attn layers' decode path.\",\n34\t    \"kb_evidence\": [],\n35\t    \"pr_evidence\": [],\n36\t    \"source_evidence\": [\n37\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/config/vllm.py:207-216 (enable_qk_norm_rope_kvcache), :225-310 (default-False at all opt levels)\",\n38\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/config/compilation.py:1356-1367 (is_custom_op_enabled), :272-295 (ROCm ok), :956-963 (+rotary_embedding append)\",\n39\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/compilation/passes/pass_manager.py:207-210 (QkNormRopeKvcacheFusionPass registration)\",\n40\t      \"/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/v1/attention/backends/rocm_aiter_unified_attn.py:312-315,333 (fused_qk_norm_rope_kvcache_supported=rocm_aiter_ops.is_enabled(); impl)\"\n41\t    ],\n42\t    \"extra_args\": \"--attention-backend ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN --compilation-config {\\\"cudagraph_mode\\\":\\\"FULL_DECODE_ONLY\\\",\\\"pass_config\\\":{\\\"fuse_qk_norm_rope_kvcache\\\":true},\\\"custom_ops\\\":[\\\"none\\\",\\\"+sparse_attn_indexer\\\",\\\"+rotary_embedding\\\"]}\",\n43\t    \"remove_args\": [\"--compilation-config\"],\n44\t    \"args_mode\": \"append\",\n45\t    \"atomic\": true\n46\t   },\n47\t   {\n48\t    \"name\": \"bridge-gdn-decode-aiter-noninterleaved-layout\",\n49\t    \"reason\": \"Bridge candidate for the freeform patcher (no config knob exists): _forward_core_rocm dispatches to the AITER fused GDN decode fast path (fused conv1d-update + fused_rearrange_sigmoid_gated_delta_rule,